---
title: Writing callouts
summary: The three callout types, and a video walkthrough.
order: 2
---

Callouts hold a short paragraph or a list. Use them sparingly: one per section at most.

{% callout %}
A callout with no attributes uses the default type, which is a note.
{% /callout %}

{% callout type="warning" title="Don't stack them" %}
Two callouts in a row read as noise. Merge them, or make one of them ordinary text.
{% /callout %}

